  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
        <Accordion title="What does pro-rata mean?">
          <p>
            Pro-rata means "in proportion". Your salary is scaled in line with the hours or days you work compared with a full-time equivalent role, so part-time staff earn a fair share of the full-time salary.
          </p>
        </Accordion>
        <Accordion title="How do I calculate my pro-rata salary?">
          <p>
            Divide the full-time salary by the full-time hours (or days) per week, then multiply by your actual hours (or days) per week. For example: (£30,000 ÷ 37.5) × 20 = £16,000.
          </p>
        </Accordion>
        <Accordion title="Do part-time workers get the same annual leave as full-time staff?">
          <p>
            Part-time workers are entitled to a pro-rated version of the 28 statutory days (including bank holidays). Use the same ratio — your hours divided by full-time hours, multiplied by 28 — as this calculator does.
          </p>
        </Accordion>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

